The Open POSIX Test Suite
=========================

dist/ is testcases/open_posix_testsuite of the Linux Test Project, release
20250130:

  https://github.com/linux-test-project/ltp/releases/download/20250130/ltp-full-20250130.tar.xz
  sha256 02e4ec326be54c3fd92968229a468c02c665d168a8a673edc38a891f7395ae10

Only conformance/, functional/, include/, tools/ and the top-level notices
are kept; upstream's GNU Makefiles, autoconf files and stress/ are not.  The
code is GPLv2+ (COPYING); it is never linked into anything shipped, and the
release build does not build it.

releasetools/posixsuite.py cross-compiles the tests on the build host against
a destdir and packs them onto a disk image; releasetools/qemutest.py runs that
image with --suite posix.  A test that does not compile is a result, not a
build failure: usually the interface it tests is missing.  See
releasetools/qemutest-posix.xfail for the known failures.

Local changes to dist/, to carry over to a newer release:

  include/affinity.h: set_affinity_single() for MINIX, which upstream
  implements for Linux only ("Must be ported to OS's other than Linux"),
  so that the tests that run on a single CPU when they can do.

To update: unpack a newer LTP release, replace dist/ with the same
directories, apply the local changes above again, update the version and
checksum here, and rebaseline.
